# Additions to /srv/icos/etc/icos.env for VPS sovereignty. NO SECRET IN THIS FILE.
# Merge by hand (owner), never by automation; keep a dated .bak of icos.env first.
#
# Without these three, the code falls back to one developer's Mac paths
# (src/server/workspace-manager/guards.ts: /Users/coco/icos, /Users/coco/icos-worktrees)
# or refuses repository-reading tasks (activities.ts: ICOS_WORKSPACE_ROOT manquant).

# Canonical repository on the VPS (the `main` checkout). Writers never run here.
ICOS_REPO_PATH=/srv/icos/repo
# Where governed worker worktrees are created (exists, owned by icos, currently empty).
ICOS_WORKER_WORKSPACE_ROOT=/srv/icos/workers
# Checkout that read-only "inspect the codebase" tasks are bound to inside the sandbox.
ICOS_WORKSPACE_ROOT=/srv/icos/repo

# The executor the worker launches. Deliberately NOT filled in: which runtime runs
# autonomous work (Claude Code via the W10 executor, Hermes, Codex) is an owner decision,
# and none of hermes/codex is installed on the VPS today. Format: exec-command-config.ts.
# ICOS_WORKER_EXEC_COMMANDS=

# Optional, recommended once the worker is live: isolate production workflows from the
# integration suites that share the same Temporal server (see audit, risk R3). Requires
# `temporal operator namespace create icos-prod` first, then the SAME value for icos-web and
# the worker (both read this file).
# TEMPORAL_NAMESPACE=icos-prod
